The two operations requests aren't included. This node's only authority is `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need filesystem access, and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need `aap:caps/http-client`. Neither is granted, and the target has no WASI. Adding either would also send untrusted feed text to places the graph never approved.

To get them, the graph would need to grant the capabilities. For example, an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` on this node, or a separate logging or enrichment node with its own `with` clause. Input logging may also be better done by the host runtime at the node boundary, where it needs no extra authority in the guest. The files below do only what the node's declared authority allows.

